[[SECTION]]
PREFIX: TC-H1FWMCBOOT-
TITLE: Test Protocol

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMCBOOT-6
TITLE: Functional1
STATEMENT: >>>
The main control bootloader firmware shall execute the primary application only when its MCUboot
header, SHA-256 hash, and ECDSA P-256 signature are valid.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. The system is ready to start.
2. A valid signed primary image is present.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Enter serial recovery and upload an intentionally invalid or unsigned image to secondary slot 1.
2. Verify image list does not report the uploaded image as a valid slot-1 image.
3. Reset the system.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. The invalid image is not accepted for upgrade.
2. The valid primary image remains selected.
3. The system boots the valid primary application.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMCBOOT-1
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMCBOOT-8
TITLE: Functional 2
STATEMENT: >>>
The main control bootloader firmware shall upload a signed MCUboot image to the secondary image slot.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. The system is ready to start.
2. A valid signed `.mcumgr.bin` image is available.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Enter serial recovery.
2. Upload the signed image using mcumgr direct image target 2.
3. Request image list.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. The mcumgr upload completes successfully.
2. Image list reports the signed image in slot 1 with `bootable: true` and a hash.
3. The primary slot is not overwritten by the upload.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMCBOOT-3
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMCBOOT-9
TITLE: Functional 3
STATEMENT: >>>
The main control bootloader firmware shall progressively erase only secondary-slot sectors needed for an image upload.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. The system is ready to start.
2. A valid signed `.mcumgr.bin` image is available.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Enter serial recovery.
2. Start a secondary-slot image upload and interrupt it before completion.
3. Reset the system.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. The incomplete secondary image is not selected.
2. The primary application remains bootable.
3. The system starts the primary application after reset.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMCBOOT-4
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMCBOOT-10
TITLE: PC Communication
STATEMENT: >>>
The main control bootloader firmware shall respond to an mcumgr echo command while serial recovery is active.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. The system is ready to start.
2. A valid signed primary image is present.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Send `*BOOTL\n` to the running application at 115200 baud.
2. Connect mcumgr at 115200 baud.
3. Send `mcumgr echo ping`.
4. Reset without sending another bootloader request.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. The application requests serial recovery and resets.
2. mcumgr communication is established.
3. The bootloader replies with `ping`.
4. The next reset boots the primary application normally.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMCBOOT-5
  ROLE: Verifies

